    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0552" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1371.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <p>In further reply to the memorandum of the Embassy of Mexico, of February 16,
                    1911, in regard to reports that one Richard Ferris was organizing a force in
                    California to invade Mexican territory, the Department of State has the honor to
                    inclose for the embassy’s information a copy of a letter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d676-f1"/> from the Assistant Attorney General, transmitting a
                    report concerning the matter from Special Agent Herrington, of the Department of
                    Justice, from which it appears that sufficient evidence against Ferris to
                    convict him of violating the neutrality laws has not been obtained.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
